    "result_text": "All green. The full build (which recompiles every main source, including the regenerated `OwnerDto`, and runs the one test class) succeeds, and the new acceptance test passes.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented `telephoneDisplay` on the Owner read model \u2014 the stored E.164 number formatted for humans (`+61412345678` \u2192 `+61 412 345 678`), while `telephone` stays raw E.164.\n\nFollowing the codebase's established convention that every derived Owner field is a `@Transient` getter mapped automatically to the DTO by MapStruct and declared as a `readOnly` property in `openapi.yml`, I:\n\n1. **Moved `E164CountryCode`** from `rest.controller` to the `model` package (made public), so the calling-code knowledge can be reused by both the existing `TelephoneNormalizer` and the new display formatting rather than being duplicated. Updated `TelephoneNormalizer` with the import.\n\n2. **Added `TelephoneFormatter`** (`model`) \u2014 a small single-responsibility helper, matching the style of `LuhnCheckDigit`/`LocalityResolver`, that splits the calling code (via `E164CountryCode`) and groups the national digits in threes. Numbers with an unrecognized calling code (unknown split boundary) are returned unchanged rather than crashing.\n\n3. **Added `Owner.getTelephoneDisplay()`** \u2014 a `@Transient` getter delegating to `TelephoneFormatter`, placed next to the raw telephone accessors.\n\n4. **Declared `telephoneDisplay`** as a `readOnly` string on the `Owner` schema in `openapi.yml`, so the generated `OwnerDto` gains the field and MapStruct wires the getter through with no mapper changes.\n\nNo formatting logic leaked into the controller or entity; each piece sits in its own unit, and the calling-code table is defined once.",
